msgstr ""

msgid "Download speed after quota (kbit/s)"
msgstr ""

msgid "After the matching quota is reached, use this speed. Empty or 0 uses native deauthentication instead of throttling."
msgstr ""

msgid "Preemptively authenticated devices"
msgstr ""

msgid "Use mac=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF;sessiontimeout=60;uploadrate=100;downloadrate=1000;uploadquota=0;downloadquota=0;custom=device. Unlike trusted MACs, these devices retain counters, quotas and timeouts. Empty or 0 quota parameters inherit global values. Custom data accepts letters, digits and _ . : @ + / -."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rules before authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "Example: allow tcp port 443 to 192.0.2.10 or block all to 192.0.2.0/24. Specify all, or tcp/udp with a port; native v11 misinterprets omitted protocols. Addresses may be IPv4, subnets or single-address hostnames."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rules after authentication"
msgstr ""

msgid "Rules follow native ordering. Defining entries replaces the native default allow-all policy; include the required allow rules."
msgstr ""

msgid "Rules for access to the router"
msgstr ""

msgid "Example: allow tcp port 8080. Native DNS, DHCP, SSH and HTTPS management rules remain included. These entries do not override a firewall passthrough configuration."
msgstr ""

msgid "Status and error page script"
msgstr ""

msgid "Empty uses the native status page. Explicit paths survive saving Portal Studio branding. The script must exist and be executable on the router."
msgstr ""

